Teams that adopt AI coding tools without a framework hit the same wall after a few months. The AI is fast, but it's generic. On the backend it doesn't know that your team wraps EF Core queries in the service layer, not the controller, that you use FluentValidation rather than DataAnnotations, or about the tech debt in the payments module you've been carefully routing around. On the frontend it doesn't know that you use signals over BehaviorSubject, that you've deprecated NgModules, that you have a house rule against nested subscribes, or about the component that can't use `OnPush` because of a third-party library quirk. It doesn't know that the last three PRs introduced async voids and memory leaks that nobody caught in review.